{
  "title": "Immature tissue and differentiation",
  "sources": "14:4,6,8",
  "stages": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "title": "Development",
      "text": "Childhood cancer is not simply adult cancer occurring earlier. The supplied chapter emphasizes immature tissues and developmental origins."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.72,
      "title": "Diverging states",
      "text": "Compare two paths. In one, immature cells mature and differentiate. In the embryonal-tumor model, tissue fails to differentiate and retains an immature pattern."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.9,
      "title": "Scope",
      "text": "Many childhood cancers arise from mesodermal tissues. Growth timing, inherited factors and exposures belong to the same assessment; no single factor explains every case."
    }
  ],
